cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'PolyCarp: condition-aware prediction of copolymer architecture'
abstract: 'PolyCarp predicts whether a radical copolymerisation gives an alternating, random to block-like or gradient copolymer. A gradient-boosted classifier reads XTB descriptors of the two monomers, the solvent log P, the temperature and the polymerisation type, and a voting layer compares its answer with the closest same-monomer reaction in a database of 3,791 copolymerisations extracted from 1,206 publications. This repository holds the web frontend; the predictions are served by the copolymer-reactivity backend.'
